IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `psa93-types`

-- Pension Schemes Act 1993 (UK) — GOAL 1: EARLY LEAVERS (ss 71, 101AA,
-- 101AB).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1993-48.txt.

§ `Goal 1 — early leavers`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day before` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

-- Earlier counting service is placed before the latest period, so the
-- totals in ss 71(7) and 101AA(2) are measured from an adjusted start.
GIVEN l IS A `Leaver facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the adjusted start of service for` l MEANS
    Date (Day (l's `pensionable service began on`) MINUS l's `earlier counting service, in days`)

GIVEN l IS A `Leaver facts`, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the leaver` l `has at least` n `months of service` IF
    l's `pensionable service ended on` AT LEAST `the last day of the` n `months beginning with` (`the adjusted start of service for` l)

-- s 71(1) "(a) he has at least 2 years' qualifying service, (aa) he has at
-- least 30 days' qualifying service and ... all of it would necessarily be
-- money purchase benefit, or (b) a transfer payment in respect of his rights
-- under a personal pension scheme has been made to the scheme". (11): (aa)
-- does not apply if any relevant service began before s 36 PA 2014 came into
-- force.
@ref s 71(1), (7), (10)-(11)
@export Whether an early leaver is entitled to short service benefit under s 71 of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (UK): pensionable service ended before normal pension age, with at least 2 years' qualifying service; or at least 30 days where all the benefit would be money purchase and no relevant service began before s 36 of the Pensions Act 2014 came into force; or a transfer payment from a personal pension scheme was received. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN l IS A `Leaver facts`  @desc The service dates, earlier counting service, the kind of benefit and any personal pension transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to short service benefit` l IF
    -- "pensionable service is terminated before normal pension age" (added
    -- after the independent pass, L20, L22).
        l's `pensionable service ended on` LESS THAN l's `reaches normal pension age on`
    AND (   `the leaver` l `has at least` 24 `months of service`
         OR (    l's `all benefit would be money purchase`
             AND NOT (l's `relevant service began before s 36 PA 2014 commenced`)
             AND l's `pensionable service ended on` AT LEAST Date (Day (`the adjusted start of service for` l) PLUS 29))
         OR l's `a personal pension transfer was received`)

-- s 71(3): short service benefit must be payable from an age no greater than
-- 65, or normal pension age if greater.
@ref s 71(3)
GIVEN l IS A `Leaver facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the latest age from which short service benefit is payable for` l MEANS
    IF l's `normal pension age, in years` GREATER THAN 65 THEN l's `normal pension age, in years` ELSE 65

-- s 101AA(1)-(2): the member leaves before normal pension age, "the three
-- month condition is satisfied, but he does not have relevant accrued rights"
-- (i.e. no short service benefit). s 101AB(1): a right to a cash transfer
-- sum or a contribution refund.
@ref ss 101AA(1)-(2), 101AB(1)
@export Whether an early leaver has the right under s 101AB of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (UK) to elect a cash transfer sum or a contribution refund: they left before normal pension age with at least three months' pensionable service (counting earlier counting service) but no entitlement to short service benefit. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN l IS A `Leaver facts`  @desc The service dates, earlier counting service, normal pension age, and the facts for short service benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may elect a cash transfer sum or contribution refund` l IF
        l's `pensionable service ended on` LESS THAN l's `reaches normal pension age on`
    AND `the leaver` l `has at least` 3 `months of service`
    AND NOT (`is entitled to short service benefit` l)

-- s 101AB(4) "a sum representing the aggregate of— (a) the member's employee
-- contributions to the scheme, and (b) [for transfer credits] the member's
-- employee contributions to that other scheme, so far as they (i) relate to
-- the transfer payment, and (ii) do not, in aggregate, exceed the amount of
-- the transfer payment."
@ref s 101AB(4)
@export The contribution refund under s 101AB(4) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (UK): the member's employee contributions, plus their employee contributions to another scheme relating to a transfer payment, up to the amount of that payment. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN l IS A `Leaver facts`  @desc The employee contributions, and any transfer-related contributions and the transfer payment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contribution refund for` l MEANS
        l's `employee contributions`
    PLUS (IF   other AT MOST l's `the transfer payment`
          THEN other
          ELSE l's `the transfer payment`)
    WHERE
        other MEANS l's `employee contributions to another scheme relating to a transfer payment`
